What this fragment does
  * a git-faithful reader of `git config --null --list` entries that keeps
    git's NULL value (a bare key) distinct from an empty value;
  * a git-faithful boolean parser that returns None for a value git itself
    rejects (git dies on it) instead of coercing it to false/true;
  * promisor_backed(repo): the classification git itself uses (does the
    repository have at least one promisor remote);
  * removal of the r23 wholesale refusal of promisor-marked repositories.

What this fragment deliberately does NOT do
  * the policy for a missing required object in a promisor-backed
    repository (exit 2 vs. verdict) is left to the integrator under
    preregistration.json expected_after[2..4];
  * GIT_ISOLATION, fetch/signature suppression, deadlines and everything
    outside the classification are untouched.

